# Phase 11: Runtime Integration — P0 (Unlocks All Value)
# Status: ACTIVE — feedback loop wired, pipeline learning from live traffic
# Depends on: Phases 1-10 (COMPLETE)
# Blocks: Phases 12-14 (partially unblocked — persistence can start)

## Goal
Wire ContextPipeline::run() into the agentic loop so every LLM request
flows through Plan→Bind→Optimize→Serialize instead of inline assembly.

## Strategy: Shadow-first rollout
1. Build ContextSources from AgenticLoopState (adapter layer)
2. Shadow-run pipeline alongside existing path (compare outputs)
3. Flip traffic when shadow diff is zero for N turns
4. Remove legacy path (deferred to Phase 14)

## Tasks

### 11.1 — ContextSources Adapter (astra-turn-core) ✅ DONE
- [x] PipelineSession as session-scoped orchestrator (owns all cross-turn state)
- [x] TurnInput/AdaptiveTurnInput structs for runtime to provide per-turn data
- [x] EmergentContext lifecycle: push_emergent_skill/memory/summary methods
- [x] SessionLatches lifecycle: latch_header/cache_scope/feature methods
- [x] PipelineStats carried across turns via PipelineSession ownership
- [x] Unit tests: 19 tests covering all lifecycle paths

### 11.2 — Pipeline Call Site (agentic_loop_turn.rs) ✅ FEEDBACK ACTIVE
- [x] PipelineSession provides run_turn() and run_turn_adaptive() entry points
- [x] record_feedback() with section usage tracking
- [x] OptimizeLimits::for_tier() auto-derives limits from pressure tier
- [x] PipelineSession field on AgenticLoopState (11 construction sites)
- [x] CLI main loop initializes PipelineSession (active from first turn)
- [x] Execution phase records feedback after every successful ingest
- [ ] Shadow mode: run pipeline alongside existing path, diff outputs (Phase 14 prereq)
